    "After 2008 the economic crisis and very high youth unemployment made many Greeks leave once more. According to Bank of Greece data, from early 2008 to mid-2016 more than 427,000 people aged 15 to 64 left the country to settle permanently abroad; in 2013 alone about 100,000 left, triple the earlier yearly average. Commentators call it the third great wave of Greek emigration, after the one to America around 1900 and the one to Germany and Australia after the Second World War.",
