    "For many children of the diaspora, Greek is the language of grandmother, of church and of the afternoon school. Afternoon and Saturday schools, usually run by communities and parishes, are the most common form of Greek education abroad; in the USA, Canada and Australia there are also Greek day schools, where children learn in both languages. In Melbourne, for example, the Archdiocese merged its parish schools in 2022 into a single college that teaches on weekday afternoons and Saturday mornings in more than a dozen suburbs.",
