    "For decades, most Greeks abroad who wanted to vote had to travel to Greece. In the European elections of June 2024, Greeks living abroad voted by post for the first time: registered voters received the ballot papers in the mail and sent their envelope back to a special committee at the courts, while voters inside Greece could choose between the post and the polling station. Some 800,000 Greeks abroad were estimated to be eligible to register.",
